# reading_translation = Often Scyld Scefing deprived enemy troops, many peoples, of mead-benches; he terrified the earls, after he was first found destitute. He experienced consolation for that; he grew under the clouds, prospered in honours, until each of the neighbouring peoples across the whale-road had to obey him and pay tribute. That was a good king!
