# sent_id = beowulf.00023
# text = -- Swā ðā drihtguman drēamum lifdon, ēadiglīce, oð ðæt ān ongan fyrene fre(m)man fēond on helle; wæs se grimma gǣst Grendel hāten, mǣre mearcstapa, sē þe mōras hēold, fen ond fæsten; fīfelcynnes eard wonsǣlī wer weardode hwīle, siþðan him Scyppend forscrifen hæfde in Cāines cynne -- þone cwealm gewræc ēce Drihten, þæs þe hē Ābel slōg; ne gefeah hē þǣre fǣhðe, ac hē hine feor forwræc, Metod for þȳ māne mancynne fram.
# ref = 98-110
# source_version = perseus-ang1
# base_analysis = Giuseppe Brunetti
# dependency_model = deepseek-chat
# reading_translation = Thus those noble retainers lived in joys, blessedly, until one began to commit crimes, a fiend in hell; that grim spirit was called Grendel, a famous prowler of the borderlands, who held the moors, the fen and the fastness; the unhappy man occupied the land of the race of monsters for a time, after the Creator had condemned him among Cain's race — the eternal Lord avenged that murder, because he slew Abel; he did not rejoice in that feud, but God banished him far from mankind for that crime.
# literal_translation = Thus then the retainers in joys lived, blessedly, until one began crimes to commit, fiend in hell; was that grim spirit Grendel called, famous border-prowler, he who moors held, fen and fastness; of monster-race land the unhappy man occupied for a time, after him the Creator condemned had in Cain's race — that murder avenged eternal Lord, because he Abel slew; not rejoiced he in that feud, but he him far banished, God for that crime from mankind.
