# sent_id = beowulf.00081
# text = Wulfgār maþelode --þæt wæs Wendla lēod, wæs his mōdsefa manegum gecȳðed, wīg ond wīsdōm --: 'Ic þæs wine Deniga, frēan Scildinga frīnan wille, bēaga bryttan, swā þū bēna eart, þēoden mǣrne ymb þīnne sīð, ond þē þā andsware ǣdre gecȳðan, ðē mē se gōda āgifan þenceð.'
# ref = 348-355
# source_version = perseus-ang1
# base_analysis = Giuseppe Brunetti
# dependency_model = deepseek-chat
# reading_translation = Wulfgar spoke — that was a man of the Vandals, his courage was made known to many, his prowess and wisdom: 'I will ask the friend of the Danes, the lord of the Scyldings, the dispenser of rings, as you are a petitioner, the famous prince about your undertaking, and swiftly make known to you the answer, which the good one intends to give me.'
# literal_translation = Wulfgar spoke -- that was of the Vandals a man, was his courage to many made known, prowess and wisdom --: 'I of that friend of Danes, lord of Scyldings ask will, of rings dispenser, as you petitioner are, prince famous about your undertaking, and to you the answer swiftly make known, which to me the good one to give intends.'
