# text = Hwīlum cyninges þegn, guma gilphlæden, gidda gemyndig, sē ðe ealfela ealdgesegena worn gemunde --word ōþer fand sōðe gebunden-- secg eft ongan sīð Bēowulfes snyttrum styrian, ond on spēd wrecan spel gerāde, wordum wrixlan; wēlhwylc gecwæð, þæt hē fram Sigemunde[s] secgan hȳrde ellendǣdum, uncūþes fela, Wælsinges gewin, wīde sīðas, þāra þe gumena bearn gearwe ne wiston, fǣhðe ond fyrena, būton Fitela mid hine, þonne hē swulces hwæt secgan wolde, eam his nefan, swā hīe ā wǣron æt nīða gehwām nȳdgesteallan; hæfdon ealfela eotena cynnes sweordum gesǣged.
# ref = 867-884
# source_version = perseus-ang1
# base_analysis = Giuseppe Brunetti
# dependency_model = deepseek-chat
# reading_translation = At times the king's retainer, a man laden with boasts, mindful of tales, who remembered a great many old legends, found other words truly bound together. The man again began to treat of Beowulf's exploit with skill, and to recite an apt tale with success, to exchange words; everything he said, that he had heard tell about Sigemund, of deeds of courage, much of the unknown, the struggle of Wælsing, distant journeys, of which the sons of men did not at all know, feud and crimes, except for Fitela with him, when he wished to say something of such matters, uncle to his nephew, as they were always companions in need in every conflict; they had laid low a great many of the race of giants with swords.
# literal_translation = At-times king's retainer, man boast-laden, of-tales mindful, he who a-great-many of-old-legends a-great-number remembered -- word other found truly bound -- man again began exploit Beowulf's with-skills to-treat, and with success to-recite tale apt, with-words to-exchange; everything said, that he about Sigemund say heard of-deeds-of-courage, of-unknown much, Wælsing's struggle, distant journeys, of-those which of-men sons at-all not knew, feud and of-crimes, except-for Fitela with him, when he of-such something say would, uncle his nephew, as they always were at of-conflicts each companions-in-need; had a-great-many of-giants of-race with-swords laid-low.
