# reading_translation = Then the protector of warriors ordered eight horses with gold-plated bridles to be led onto the hall floor, inside under the precincts; on one of them stood a saddle decorated with skill, adorned with treasure; that was the war-seat of the high king, when the son of Healfdene wished to perform the play of swords -- never in the vanguard did the prowess of the widely known one fail, when the slain fell.
