# sent_id = beowulf.00337
# text = Hē æt wīge gecrang ealdres scyldig, ond nū ōþer cwōm mihtig mānscaða, wolde hyre mǣg wrecan, gē feor hafað fǣhðe gestǣled, þæs þe þincean mæg þegne monegum, sē þe æfter sincgyfan on sefan grēoteþ,-- hreþerbealo hearde; nū sēo hand ligeð, sē þe ēow wēlhwylcra wilna dohte.
# ref = 1337-1344
# source_version = perseus-ang1
# base_analysis = Giuseppe Brunetti
# dependency_model = deepseek-chat
# reading_translation = He fell in battle, having forfeited his life, and now another has come, a mighty wicked assailant, who wished to avenge her kinsman; and she has far pursued the feud, as may seem to many a retainer who, after the treasure-giver, grieves in his heart -- hard distress of soul; now the hand lies low, which was able to gratify every one of your desires.
# literal_translation = He at war fell, of life forfeiting, and now other came, mighty wicked-assailant, wished her kinsman to avenge; and far has the feud avenged, as may seem to many a retainer, he who after treasure-giver in heart weeps -- heart-distress hard; now the hand lies, which to you of every desire was able.
