# sent_id = beowulf.00370
# text = Næs þæt þonne mǣtost mægenfultuma, þæt him on ðearfe lāh ðyle Hrōðgþares; wæs þǣm hæftmēce Hrunting nama; þæt wæs ān foran ealdgestrēona; ecg wæs īren, ātertānum fāh, āhyrded heaþoswāte; nǣfre hit æt hilde ne swāc manna ǣngum þāra þe hit mid mundum bewand, sē ðe gryresīðas gegān dorste, folcstede fāra; næs þæt forma sīeth;, þæt hit ellenweorc æfnan scolde.
# ref = 1455-1464
# source_version = perseus-ang1
# base_analysis = Giuseppe Brunetti
# dependency_model = deepseek-chat
# reading_translation = That was then no least of mighty helps, that the spokesman of Hrothgar lent him in need; the hilted sword was named Hrunting; that was one of the foremost ancient treasures; its blade was iron, gleaming with poison-stripes, hardened in battle-blood; never in battle did it fail any man of those who grasped it with hands, who dared to enter upon perilous expeditions, the meeting-place of enemies; that was not the first time that it had to perform a deed of courage.
# literal_translation = Not-was that then least of mighty-help, that to-him in need lent spokesman Hrothgar's; was the hilted-sword Hrunting name; that was one of foremost ancient-treasures; edge was iron, with-poison-stripes gleaming, hardened with-battle-sweat; never it in battle not failed of-men any of-those who it with hands grasped, he who perilous-expeditions to-enter dared, meeting-place of-enemies; not-was that first time, that it courageous-deed perform had-to.
