# text = Hūru ne gemunde mago Ecglāfes eafoþes cræftig, þæt hē ǣr gespræc wīne druncen, þā hē þæs wǣpnes onlāh sēlran sweordfrecan; selfa ne dorste under ȳða gewin aldre genēþan, drihtscype drēogan; þǣr hē dōme forlēas, ellenmǣrðum.
# ref = 1465-1471
# source_version = perseus-ang1
# base_analysis = Giuseppe Brunetti
# dependency_model = deepseek-chat
# reading_translation = Indeed, the son of Ecglaf, powerful in strength, did not remember what he had said before, drunk with wine, when he lent that weapon, a better sword to the warrior; he himself did not dare to venture his life under the turmoil of waves, to perform deeds of valor; there he lost glory, reputation for courage.
# literal_translation = Indeed not remembered son of Ecglaf of strength powerful, that he before said wine drunk, when he that weapon lent better sword-warrior; himself not dared under of-waves turmoil life to-venture, deed-of-valour to-perform; there he glory lost, reputation-for-courage.
