# reading_translation = And you, Unferth, let the old heirloom, the wondrous wave-patterned sword, the widely known man, the hard-edged blade, be had; I shall achieve glory for myself with Hrunting, or death shall take me. After those words the man of the Weder-Geats hastened with courage—not at all did he wish to await an answer; the surging water received the warrior.
