# sent_id = beowulf.00418
# text = Ðā wæs gylden hilt gamelum rince, hārum hildfruman on hand gyfen, enta ǣrgeweorc; hit on ǣht gehwearf æfter dēofla hryre Denigea frean, wundorsmiþa geweorc; ond þā þās worold ofgeaf gromheort guma, Godes andsaca, morðres scyldig, ond his mōdor ēac; on geweald gehwearf woroldcyninga ðǣm sēlestan be sǣm twēonum ðāra þe on Scedenigge sceattas dǣlde.
# ref = 1677-1686
# source_version = perseus-ang1
# base_analysis = Giuseppe Brunetti
# dependency_model = deepseek-chat
# reading_translation = Then the golden hilt, the ancient work of giants, was given into the hand of the old warrior, the hoary war-leader; after the demons' fall it passed into the possession of the lord of the Danes, the handiwork of wonder-smiths; and then that hostile-hearted man, God's adversary, guilty of murder, gave up this world, and his mother also; it passed into the power of the best of earthly kings between the two seas, of those who distributed treasures in Scandia.
# literal_translation = Then was golden hilt to old warrior, to hoary war-leader in hand given, giants' ancient-work; it into possession passed after demons' fall to Danes' lord, of wonder-smiths handiwork; and then this world gave-up hostile-hearted man, God's adversary, of murder guilty, and his mother also; into power passed of earthly-kings to-the best between seas two of-those who in Scandia treasures distributed.
