# sent_id = beowulf.00419
# text = Hrōðgār maðelode-- hylt scēawode, ealde lāfe, on ðǣm wæs ōr writen fyrngewinnes; syðþan flōd ofslōh, gifen gēotende gīganta cyn, frēcne gefērdon; þæt wæs fremde þēod ēcean Dryhtne; him þæs endelēan þurh wæteres wylm Waldend sealde.
# ref = 1687-1693
# source_version = perseus-ang1
# base_analysis = Giuseppe Brunetti
# dependency_model = deepseek-chat
# reading_translation = Hrothgar spoke — he examined the hilt, the ancient heirloom, on which the origin of ancient strife was engraved; after the flood, the rushing sea, slew the race of giants — they fared terribly; that people was alien to the eternal Lord; the Ruler gave them a final reward through the surging of water.
# literal_translation = Hrothgar spoke -- he examined the hilt, ancient heirloom, on which was origin engraved of ancient strife; after the flood slew, sea rushing, giants' race, terribly they fared; that was alien people to eternal Lord; to them of that final-reward through water's surge the Ruler gave.
