# sent_id = beowulf.00433
# text = þonne bið on hreþre under helm drepen biteran strǣle -- him bebeorgan ne con --, wōm wundorbebodum wergan gāstes; þinceð him tō lȳtel, þæt hē lange hēold, gȳtsað gromhȳdig, nallas on gylp seleð fǣtte bēagas, ond hē þā forðgesceaft forgyteð ond forgæymeð, þæs þe him ǣr God sealde, wuldres Waldend, weorðmynda dǣl.
# ref = 1745-1752
# source_version = perseus-ang1
# base_analysis = Giuseppe Brunetti
# dependency_model = deepseek-chat
# reading_translation = Then it is struck in the breast, under the helmet, by a sharp arrow — he cannot protect himself —, the perverse one, with the mysterious commands of the accursed spirit; it seems to him too little, what he long held; the angry-minded one covets, not at all does he give plated rings in boast, and he forgets and neglects the future destiny, because God, the Ruler of glory, formerly gave him a share of honours.
# literal_translation = Then is in breast under helmet struck by sharp arrow — himself protect not can —, perverse with mysterious commands of accursed spirit; seems to him too little, that he long held; covets angry-minded, not-at-all in boast gives plated rings, and he the future destiny forgets and neglects, because to him before God gave, of glory Ruler, of honours portion.
