# sent_id = beowulf.00478
# text = Hūru þæt onhōhsnod[e] Hemminges mǣg: ealodrincende ōðer sǣdan, þæt hīo lēodbealewa lǣs gefremede, inwitnīða, syððan ǣrest wearð gyfen goldhroden geongum cempan, æðelum dīore, syððan hīo Offan flet ofer fealone flōd be fæder lāre sīðe gesōhte; ðǣr hīo syððan well in gumstōle, gōde mǣre, līfgesceafta lifigende brēac, hīold hēahlufan wið hæleþa brego, ealles moncynnes mīne gefrǣge þone sēlestan bī sǣm twēonum, eormencynnes; forðām Offa wæs geofum ond gūðum, gārcēne man, wīde geweorðod, wīsdōme hēold ēðel sīnne;-- þonon Ēomēr wōc hæleðum tō helpe, Hem[m]inges mǣg, nefa Gārmundes, nīða cræftig.
# ref = 1944-1962
# source_version = perseus-ang1
# base_analysis = Giuseppe Brunetti
# dependency_model = deepseek-chat
# reading_translation = Indeed, that kinsman of Hemming, the ale-drinker, confirmed it: others said that she committed fewer injuries to the people, fewer hostile acts, after she was first given, gold-adorned, to the young warrior, dear in lineage, after she, by her father's counsel, sought Offa's hall across the fallow flood on a journey; there she afterwards prospered well in the throne-room, famous for goodness, living, enjoyed the life decreed by fate, held deep love for the lord of heroes, the best of all mankind between the two seas, of the mighty race, in my knowledge; therefore Offa was honoured widely with gifts and battles, a spear-bold man, he held his native land with wisdom; from him Eomer was born as a help to men, kinsman of Hemming, grandson of Garmund, powerful in assaults.
# literal_translation = Indeed that onhohsnod[e] Hemming's kinsman: ale-drinking other said, that she of people-injuries less performed, of hostile acts, after first was given gold-adorned young warrior, dear in lineage, after she Offa's hall over fallow flood by father's counsel journey sought; where she afterwards well in throne-room, good famous, of life-decrees living enjoyed, held deep-love against lord of men, of all mankind in my knowledge the best between seas two, of mighty race; therefore Offa was with gifts and battles, spear-bold man, widely honoured, with wisdom held native-land his; thence Eomer was born to men as help, Hemming's kinsman, grandson of Garmund, of assaults powerful.
