# sent_id = beowulf.00498
# text = þonne cwið æt bēore sē ðe bēah gesyhð, eald æscwiga, sē ðe eall gem(an), gārcwealm gumena -- him bið grim sefa --, onginneð geōmormōd geong(um) cempan þurh hreðra gehygd higes cunnian, wīgbealu weccean, ond þæt word ācwyð: "Meaht ðū, mīn wine, mēce gecnāwan, þone þīn fæder tō gefeohte bær under heregrīman hindeman sīðe, dȳre īren, þǣr hyne Dene slōgon, wēoldon wælstōwe, syððan Wiðergyld læg, æfter hæleþa hryre, hwate Scyldungas ?
# ref = 2041-2052
# source_version = perseus-ang1
# base_analysis = Giuseppe Brunetti
# dependency_model = deepseek-chat
# reading_translation = Then at beer he speaks, he who sees the ring, the old spear-warrior, he who remembers all, the spear-death of men -- his mind is grim --, he begins, sad of mind, through the thought of his breast to test the mind of a young warrior, to awaken war-evil, and he speaks that word: "Can you, my friend, recognize the sword, which your father bore into battle under the war-mask on his last journey, the precious iron, where the Danes struck him, held the field of slaughter, after Withergyld lay dead, after the fall of heroes, the bold Scyldings?"
# literal_translation = Then speaks at beer he who ring sees, old spear-warrior, he who all remembers, spear-death of men -- to him is grim mind --, begins sad-of-mind young warrior through breast's thought mind to test, war-evil to awaken, and that word says: "May you, my friend, sword recognize, which your father to battle bore under war-mask last time, precious iron, where him Danes struck, ruled slaughter-field, after Withergyld lay, after heroes' fall, bold Scyldings?"
