# sent_id = beowulf.00512
# text = þǣr wæs gidd ond glēo; gomela Scilding, felafricgende feorran rehte hwīlum hildedēor hearpan wynne, gomenwudu grētte, hwīlum gyd āwræc sōð ond sārlīc, hwīlum syllīc spell rehte æfter rihte rūmheort cyning; hwīlum eft ongan eldo gebunden, gomel gūðwiga gioguðe cwīðan, hildestrengo; hreðer inne wēoll, þonne hē wintrum frōd worn gemunde.
# ref = 2105-2114
# source_version = perseus-ang1
# base_analysis = Giuseppe Brunetti
# dependency_model = deepseek-chat
# reading_translation = There was song and music; the old Scylding, well informed, narrated from far back. At times the battle-brave one touched the joy of the harp, the mirth-wood; at times he recited a true and sorrowful tale; at times the large-hearted king narrated a strange story according to right. At times again the old warrior, bound by old age, began to lament his youth, his battle-strength; his heart welled within when he, wise in winters, remembered many things.
# literal_translation = There was song and music; old Scylding, well-informed, from far back narrated at times battle-brave [one] harp's joy, mirth-wood greeted, at times tale recited true and sorrowful, at times strange tale narrated according to right, large-hearted king; at times again began old age bound, old warrior youth to lament, battle-strength; heart within welled, when he in winters wise many things remembered.
