# sent_id = beowulf.00534
# text = Eft þæt geīode ufaran dōgrum hildehlæmmum, syððan Hygelāc læg, ond Hear[dr]ēde hildemēceas under bordhrēoðan tō bonan wurdon, ðā hyne gesōhtan on sigeþēode hearde hildfrecan, Heaðo-Scilfingas, nīða genǣgdan nefan Hererīces --: syððan Bēowulfe brāde rīce on hand gehwearf; hē gehēold tela fiftig wintra -- wæs ðā frōd cyning, eald ēþelweard --, oð ðæt ān ongan deorcum nihtum draca rīcs[i]an, sē ðe on hēa(um) h(ǣþ)e hord beweotode, stānbeorh stēapne; stīg under læg eldum uncūð.
# ref = 2200-2214
# source_version = perseus-ang1
# base_analysis = Giuseppe Brunetti
# dependency_model = deepseek-chat
# reading_translation = Afterwards that came to pass in later days in battle-clashes, after Hygelac lay dead, and battle-swords became deadly to Heardred beneath the shield-cover, when hardy war-wolves, the Battle-Scylfings, sought him out among the victorious people, attacked the nephew of Hereric with violence -- after the broad kingdom passed into Beowulf's hand; he held it well for fifty winters -- he was then a wise king, an old guardian of the homeland --, until one began in the dark nights to rule, a dragon, which in a high barrow watched over a hoard, a steep stone-barrow; a path lay beneath, unknown to men.
# literal_translation = Afterwards that happened in later days in battle-clashes, after Hygelac lay, and to Heardred battle-swords under shield-cover to slayer became, when him sought in victorious-people hardy war-wolves, Battle-Scylfings, with assaults attacked nephew of Hereric --: after to Beowulf broad kingdom into hand turned; he held well fifty winters -- was then wise king, old homeland-guardian --, until one began in dark nights to rule, that which in high barrow hoard watched over, stone-barrow steep; path under lay to men unknown.
