# sent_id = beowulf.00600
# text = Næs him ǣnig þearf, þæt hē tō Gifðum oððe tō Gār-Denum oððe in Swīorīce sēcean þurfe wyrsan wīgfrecan, weorðe gecȳpan; symle ic him on fēðan beforan wolde, āna on orde, ond swā tō aldre sceall sæcce fremman, þenden þis sweord þolað, þæt mec ǣr ond sīð oft gelǣste, syððan ic for dugeðum Dæghrefne wearð tō handbonan, Hūga cempan;-- nalles hē ðā frætwe Frēscyning[e], brēostweorðunge bringan mōste, ac in campe gecrong cumbles hyrde, æþeling on elne; ne wæs ecg bona, ac him hildegrāp heortan wylmas, bānhūs gebræc.
# ref = 2493-2508
# source_version = perseus-ang1
# base_analysis = Giuseppe Brunetti
# dependency_model = deepseek-chat
# reading_translation = There was no need for him to seek out, among the Gepidae or the Spear-Danes or in Sweden, a worse warrior, to buy with a price; always I would go before him in the troop, alone at the front, and so for life I must wage war, as long as this sword holds out, which has often served me early and late, ever since I, before the retinue, became the hand-slayer of Dæghrefn, the warrior of the Hugas; not at all could he bring the ornaments, the breast-adornment, to the Frisian king, but in battle the guardian of the standard fell, a prince in courage; the blade was not the slayer, but the battle-grip crushed the surges of his heart, the bone-house.
# literal_translation = Not-was to-him any need, that he to Gepidae or to Spear-Danes or in Sweden seek need worse warrior, price buy; always I for him in foot-troop before would, alone at front, and so for life shall war wage, while this sword holds out, which me before and after often served, after I before retinue Dæghrefn became to hand-slayer, Hugas' warrior; not-at-all he then ornaments Frisian-king, breast-adornment bring might, but in battle fell standard's guardian, prince in courage; not was blade slayer, but him battle-grip heart's surges, bone-house crushed.
