# text = Gegrētte ðā gumena gehwylcne, hwate helmberend hindeman sīðe, swǣse gesīðas: 'Nolde ic sweord beran, wǣpen tō wyrme, gif ic wiste hū wið ðām āglǣcean elles meahte gylpe wiðgrīpan, swā ic giō wið Grendle dyde; ac ic ðǣr heaðufȳres hātes wēne, [o]reðes ond attres; forðon ic mē on hafu bord ond byrnan.
# ref = 2516-2524
# source_version = perseus-ang1
# base_analysis = Giuseppe Brunetti
# dependency_model = deepseek-chat
# reading_translation = Then he greeted each of the men, bold helmet-bearers, for the last time, his dear companions: 'I would not carry a sword, a weapon against the serpent, if I knew how I might otherwise grapple in glory with that adversary, as I formerly did against Grendel; but there I expect hot deadly fire, fierce and venomous; therefore I have on me shield and mail-coat.'
# literal_translation = Greeted then of-men each, bold helmet-bearer, last time, dear companions: 'Not-would I sword bear, weapon against serpent, if I knew how with that adversary otherwise might with-glory grapple, as I formerly with Grendel did; but I there of-deadly-fire hot expect, fierce and of-venom; therefore I me on have shield and mail-coat.'
