# sent_id = beowulf.00627
# text = Gemunde ðā ðā āre, þē hē him ǣr forgeaf, wīcstede weligne Wǣgmundinga, folcrihta gehwylc, swā his fæder āhte; ne mihte ðā forhabban, bond rond gefēng, geolwe linde, gomel swyrd getēah; þæt wæs mid eldum Ēanmundes lāf, suna Ōhtere[s] ; þām æt sæcce wearð, wræcca(n) winelēasum Wēohstān bana mēces ecgum, ond his māgum ætbær brūnfāgne helm, hringde byrnan, ealdsweord etonisc; þæt him Onela forgeaf, his gædelinges gūðgewǣdu, fyrdsearo fūslīc,-- nō ymbe ðā fǣhðe spræc, þēah ðe hē his brōðor bearn ābredwade.
# ref = 2606-2619
# source_version = perseus-ang1
# base_analysis = Giuseppe Brunetti
# dependency_model = deepseek-chat
# reading_translation = Then he remembered the honor that he had earlier granted him, the rich dwelling-place of the Wægmundings, every right of the people, as his father had possessed; then he could not hold back, he grasped the shield, the yellow linden-wood, drew the ancient sword; that was among men Eanmund's heirloom, the son of Ohtere; to him in battle, the friendless exile, Weohstan became slayer with the edges of the sword, and to his kinsmen he brought the burnished helmet, the ringed mail-coat, the ancient giant-made sword; that Onela gave him, his kinsman's war-garments, ready war-gear — he did not speak at all about the feud, though he had struck down his brother's son.
# literal_translation = Remembered then the honor, which he to him before granted, dwelling-place rich of Wægmundings, people-rights each, as his father possessed; not could then hold back, bond shield grasped, yellow linden, ancient sword drew; that was among men Eanmund's heirloom, son of Ohtere; to that one at battle became, exile friendless, Weohstan slayer of sword with edges, and his kinsmen brought burnished helmet, ringed mail-coat, ancient-sword giant-made; that to him Onela granted, his kinsman's war-garments, war-gear ready — not at all about the feud spoke, though he his brother's son struck down.
