# sent_id = beowulf.00631
# text = Wīglāf maðelode, wordrihta fela sægde gesīðum --him wæs sefa geōmor--: 'Ic ðæt mǣl geman, þǣr wē medu þēgun, þonne wē gehēton ūssum hlāforde in bīorsele, ðē ūs ðās bēagas geaf, þæt wē him ðā gūðgeatwa gyldan woldon, gif him þyslicu þearf gelumpe, helmas ond heard sweord.
# ref = 2631-2638
# source_version = perseus-ang1
# base_analysis = Giuseppe Brunetti
# dependency_model = deepseek-chat
# reading_translation = Wiglaf spoke, said many words of instruction to his companions -- his mind was sad --: 'I remember the occasion when we partook of mead, when we promised our lord in the beer-hall, who gave us these rings, that we would repay him for the war-gear, if such need befell him, helmets and hard swords.'
# literal_translation = Wiglaf spoke, of words-rights many said to companions -- to him was mind sad --: 'I that occasion remember, where we mead consumed, when we promised our lord in beer-hall, who us these rings gave, that we to him the war-gear repay would, if to him such need befell, helmets and hard sword.'
