# reading_translation = Little did he keep silent about new tidings, he who was not hindered, but he truly spoke before all: 'Now the joy-giver of the Weder people, the lord of the Geats, is fast on his deathbed; he occupies the slaughter-bed through the serpent's deeds; beside him lies the deadly foe, sick with dagger-wounds; with the sword he could not inflict any wound at all on that adversary.'
# literal_translation = Little was silent of new tidings he who not was hindered, but he truly said before all: 'Now is joy-giver of Weders of men, lord of Geats on death-bed fast, dwells slaughter-bed by serpent's deeds; him alongside lies deadly-foe with dagger-wounds sick; with sword not could on that adversary any of things wound inflict.'
