# base_analysis = Giuseppe Brunetti
# dependency_model = deepseek-chat
# reading_translation = He received those treasures and courteously promised rewards among the people, and fulfilled it so; the lord of the Geats, Hrethel's son, repaid that war-attack when he came home: to Eofor and Wulf with exceeding treasures he gave, to each of them a hundred thousand of land and linked rings — no man in the world needed to reproach him for that reward, after they had achieved those glorious deeds; and then to Eofor he gave his only daughter, a home-honour, as a pledge of favour.
# literal_translation = He those treasures received and him courteously promised rewards among men, and fulfilled so; repaid that war-rush of Geats lord, Hrethel's son, when he to home came, Eofor and Wulf with exceeding treasures, gave of them to each hundred thousands of land and of linked rings — not needed him those rewards to reproach man in world, after they those glorious deeds struck; and then Eofor gave only daughter, home-honour, favour as pledge.
