# sent_id = beowulf.00708
# text = þæt ys sīo fǣhðo ond se fēondscipe, wælnīð wera, ðæs ðe ic [wēn] hafo, þē ūs sēceað tō Swēona lēoda, syððan hīe gefricgeað frēan ūserne ealdorlēasne, þone ðe ǣr gehēold wið hettendum hord ond rīce, æfter hæleða hryre, hwate Sǣ-Gēatas, folcrēd fremede, oððe furður gēn eorlscipe efnde.
# ref = 2999-3007
# source_version = perseus-ang1
# base_analysis = Giuseppe Brunetti
# dependency_model = deepseek-chat
# reading_translation = That is the feud and the enmity, the deadly hostility of men, from which, as I expect, the Swedish people will seek us out, once they hear that our lord is lifeless, he who previously guarded the hoard and kingdom against enemies, after the fall of heroes, and, bold Sæ-Geatas, advanced the people's welfare, or furthermore still performed heroic deeds.
# literal_translation = That is the feud and the enmity, deadly hostility of men, of which I expectation have, that us seek to Swedes' people, after they hear lord our lifeless, him who before guarded against enemies hoard and kingdom, after fall of heroes, bold Sea-Geatas, people's-welfare furthered, or further still heroic-deed performed.
