# reading_translation = Previously they had seen there a stranger creature, a serpent lying on the plain, opposite the hateful one; the fire-dragon was fierce, variegated with gold, scorched with flames; it was fifty foot-measures long as it lay; it held the joy of the air by night at times, then went down again to seek its den; then it was fast in death, it had used up the end of its earth-cave.
# literal_translation = Previously they there saw a stranger creature, a serpent on the plain, opposite there the hateful one lying; the fire-dragon was fierce, variegated with gold, with flames scorched; that one was of fifty foot-measures long in lying; air-joy it held by night at times, down again it went the den to seek; it was then in death fast, it had of earth-caves the end enjoyed.
