# sent_id = beowulf.00731
# text = Hēt ðā gebēodan byre Wīhstānes, hæle hildedīor hæleða monegum, boldāgendra, þæt hīe bǣlwudu feorran feredon, folcāgende, gōdum tōgēnes: 'Nū sceal glēd fretan (weaxan wonna lēg) wigena strengel, þone ðe oft gebād īsernscūre, þonne strǣla storm strengum gebǣded scōc ofer scildweall, sceft nytte hēold, fæðergearwum fūs flāne fullēode.'
# ref = 3110-3119
# source_version = perseus-ang1
# base_analysis = Giuseppe Brunetti
# dependency_model = deepseek-chat
# reading_translation = Then the son of Weohstan, a man brave in battle, commanded many of the warriors, hall-owners, that they should bring wood for the funeral pyre from afar, the people's leader, for the good ones: 'Now fire shall devour the chief of warriors (the dark flame shall grow), him who often endured the iron shower, when the storm of arrows, impelled by bowstrings, shot over the shield-wall; the shaft performed its service, eager with feather-gear, it helped the arrow-head.'
# literal_translation = Ordered then to command son of-Weohstan, man battle-brave, of-men many, of-hall-owners, that they pyre-wood from-afar carry, people-leader, for-good-ones towards: 'Now shall fire devour (grow dark flame) of-warriors chief, him who often awaited iron-shower, when of-arrows storm by-strings impelled shot over shield-wall, shaft service held, with-feather-gear eager arrow-head fulfilled.'
