# reading_translation = Then around the barrow rode the battle-brave ones, sons of princes, twelve in all; they wished to lament their grief and speak of the king, recite a song, and talk about the man; they praised his nobility and judged his deeds of courage highly — as it is fitting that one should praise his lord and friend with words, love him in heart, when he must be led forth from the body.
# literal_translation = Then around the barrow rode battle-brave (ones), princes' sons, of all twelve; (they) wished (grief) to lament, and the king to speak of, a song to recite, and about the man to speak; (they) praised nobility and his courage-deeds with powers judged — as it is (fitting), that one his lord-and-friend with words praise, with hearts love, when he forth must from the body (led) be.
